WEBVTT

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:10.020
It's almost Obon. We
 should launch a leisure cruiser.

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:14.240
I wonder if Yaichiro is actually
 making the arrangements.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.900
Have you heard anything?

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:20.370
No, he hasn't said a thing.

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:25.760
I wonder if everything's going okay. 
The Manpukumaru's gone, so...

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:30.520
He doesn't have to do it alone; 
he could talk to you about it.

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:34.360
He hates asking his younger
 brothers for help, though.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:37.850
Could you please try to 
get along with him better?

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:42.180
I love my big brother! He's a great guy!

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.600
Always with the sarcasm!

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:52.610
One of the highlights of summer, 
the night of the Gozan Fire Festival.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:56.060
Matching the mood of 
the merry-making humans,

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:00.380
we tanuki throw a crazy party in the sky.

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:03.370
This uncontrollable inclination

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:05.750
has most definitely been 
inherited in an unbroken streak

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:08.800
since the long ago reign of Emperor Kammu.

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:09.080
<b>Manpukumaru</b>

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:13.560
Our deceased dad called 
this our "idiot blood."

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:48.020
<b>Episode Three: 
Yakushibo's Inner Parlor</b>

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.700
Well, that's how it is. 
Is there anything you can do?

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.480
Please arrange a leisure cruiser for us.

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:00.240
I thought you had decided to borrow 
one from someone you know in Nara?

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:03.490
It crashed on the way here...

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:07.020
This time Yaichiro messed up.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:09.780
You're the only one we can turn to now.

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:14.170
If you beg, I'll figure something out.

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:33.830
Are you kidding me?

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:45.610
Your brother is in trouble and 
you make him beg for help?

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:52.000
And that's how I got stuck 
cleaning up that furball's mess.

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:55.130
For all that you seem pretty chill.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:56.500
I have a lead.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:01.510
By the way, I heard that when 
the god of thunder showed up

00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:04.720
Kaisei saved Mother.

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:05.750
Yeah.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:08.160
How's it going with her?

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:09.390
Dunno.

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:11.630
Oh c'mon, you don't have to hide it.

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:15.910
Go on and confess everything 
to your unreliable big brother...

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:17.650
...even though I'm a frog.

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:21.740
Our engagement was decided 
entirely by Father.

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:24.740
But it seems like you're still seeing her?

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:30.720
Yeah, I have no idea what she's thinking.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.540
We haven't even really met face to face.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:38.290
How charmingly innocent. 
This green frog is about to blush red.

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:42.420
You can come up with all kinds 
of erotic fantasies if you want,

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:46.400
but it's not such smooth sailing.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:50.220
In the first place, if Uncle Ebisugawa 
became my father-in-law

00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:53.990
and Kinkaku and Ginaku, those 
dumbass twins, became my brothers,

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:55.900
it'd be a living hell.

00:04:57.340 --> 00:05:00.150
Under those circumstances I'd say
 it'd be appropriate to hole up in a well.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:03.690
You hole up in a well no matter what.

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:09.070
It must be tough for you, but 
this is something Father decided, so...

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:11.150
You can say that, but I still don't like it.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:16.420
Father must've had some 
underlying reason, though.

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:22.550
Or, it was just that he thought he could get
 some Electric Brandy under the table.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:24.450
Nah, that's ridiculous.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:27.900
No matter how much Father loved his 
booze, he wouldn't have done that.

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:32.310
Either way, Ebisugawa has 
already broken it off.

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:34.740
Get out!

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:36.810
Don't ever come back!

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:39.020
Go to hell, go to hell!

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:42.070
Go to hell, go to hell!

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:44.130
Go to hell!

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:48.740
You don't often see Mother get that angry.

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:52.450
But it was because she'd 
taken a liking to Kaisei.

00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:56.110
I wonder how long this feud's gonna last.

00:05:56.850 --> 00:06:00.960
If Father were here, he wouldn't 
let Uncle get such a big head.

00:06:01.510 --> 00:06:05.130
Certainly Father'd be able 
to handle things a bit better.

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:09.230
Well, you should just take it easy.

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:12.120
Father'd probably laugh it off.

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:22.860
<b>Port wine</b>

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:26.360
Big Brother, I can charge my phone.

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:32.420
Who do you even call?

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:34.260
Mother, of course.

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:38.290
But aren't you always with her anyways?

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:42.670
Nooo, what about when I go to the factory?

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:45.670
<b>Kyoto Gozan Fire Festival</b>

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:50.180
I wonder if Prof. Akadama 
will lend us his cruiser.

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:54.200
Well, he does hate relying on vehicles, so...

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:59.510
But he hurt his back and can't 
move around so well. He should use it!

00:07:00.130 --> 00:07:05.940
I guess he doesn't want to advertise the 
fact that he's facing a tengu identity crisis.

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:08.110
Oh, there's also <i>that</i>.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:13.360
The inner parlor runs on alcohol.

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:17.190
If he has to give his ride wine,

00:07:17.590 --> 00:07:19.510
he'd just as soon pour it into his own belly

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:23.100
and let his imagination fly 
freely through the sky instead.

00:07:28.450 --> 00:07:32.810
Yasaburo of the Shimogamos, huh. 
You've grown up magnificently.

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:37.220
Are you stupid? What's the 
point of a magnificent tanuki?

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:40.090
You're too easy on them.

00:07:40.970 --> 00:07:44.310
That's why the hairballs get so uppity.

00:07:44.990 --> 00:07:48.430
You've passed the position of 
Mount Iwayayama Tengu on to a successor?

00:07:48.970 --> 00:07:53.450
Yes, now I'm running a secondhand
 camera shop in Osaka for fun.

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:57.800
Getting obsessed with cameras 
even though you're a tengu, hmph.

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:02.310
Yakushibo says he doesn't need these, 
so you guys should have some.

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:04.730
Don't mind if we do.

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:09.720
By the way, coming here 
from Osaka by train, really?

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:12.360
You're a disgrace to all tengu.

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:16.890
You try flying in the middle 
of summer! Your brains'll boil.

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:19.680
It's cool on the Keihan Railway.

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:21.690
Just pitiful.

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:24.190
But you know, I'm surprised.

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:29.540
When I got to Demachi, I thought I'd like 
to see you and flew by Mount Nyoigatake,

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:32.670
but it was all Kurama tengu.

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:38.660
It shocked me to hear that you of all tengu 
had moved to the Demachi shopping district.

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:43.560
It was a pain in the neck so I'm having them 
take care of the whole Mount Nyoigatake area.

00:08:44.730 --> 00:08:50.600
I find it regrettable that one with the name 
Nyoigatake Yakushibo would do such a thing.

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:55.890
I can't get myself to like 
those Kurama fellows.

00:08:56.460 --> 00:08:59.910
They're gross, all pale like bean sprouts.

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:04.830
If you want to chase them off, 
I'll have my successor help you out.

00:09:04.970 --> 00:09:06.540
No thanks.

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:09.560
It's almost time for the Fire Festival.

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:14.170
I wonder if you won't feel 
homesick for your mountain.

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:18.630
If you're going to watch the fires, 
I imagine it's better from below.

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:22.910
You can't tell what's going on
 from up in the mountains.

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:25.550
Whatever you say.

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:29.170
Professor, about the Fire Festival...

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:33.460
I believe you know we launch 
a leisure cruiser each year.

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:34.910
That I do.

00:09:35.310 --> 00:09:39.020
You tanuki are idiots beyond help.

00:09:40.190 --> 00:09:43.930
Would it be possible for us to 
borrow your inner parlor?

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:47.160
"Inner parlor"?

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:48.640
Oh c'mon, you know,

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:52.690
that little flying tea room thing.

00:09:53.300 --> 00:09:55.190
Ohhh, that.

00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:58.600
Now that you mention it, 
where did I put that?

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:03.290
Ohhh, right. I gave it to Benten.

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:10.510
What the hell!

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:13.300
Why do you have to give her 
any and every last thing?

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:17.380
You gave her the Fujin Raijin 
folding fan <i>and</i> the inner parlor?

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:22.050
You can't fly, you can't whip up a whirlwind,
 why would you give up your last--

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:26.060
You still don't get it, you fool?

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:28.770
It's because I want to see her smiling face!

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:36.030
<b>Rokkaku-do</b>

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:36.030
<b>Nishizaki Genemon's Shop</b>

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:42.540
Well my lead led nowhere fast.

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:46.570
It seems like you're taking 
good care of Yakushibo.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:49.310
That's truly admirable of you.

00:10:50.340 --> 00:10:53.270
I kinda just found myself forced into it.

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:56.020
The other kids he was 
teaching don't come around.

00:10:56.670 --> 00:11:01.510
All Yakushibo does is complain, 
but there's no doubt that he <i>is</i> thankful.

00:11:02.150 --> 00:11:05.220
Please don't just say things 
to make me feel better.

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:09.680
Dang, that was pretty bad even for me.

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:15.220
I'm sure a big factor is that he hurt his back
 after falling from the Demon King Cedar.

00:11:16.390 --> 00:11:17.480
Oh, you think so?

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:23.450
If he hadn't, even considering his age, I 
think he'd be able to be a little more active

00:11:23.980 --> 00:11:27.480
and he wouldn't let those 
Kurama fellows get so cocky.

00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:29.650
By the way,

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:32.860
that Benten girl, the human,

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:37.000
is it true that she's pretty 
close with the Kurama lot as well?

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:38.550
It seems that way.

00:11:39.390 --> 00:11:46.220
Somehow I feel like she must be involved 
in the Demon King Cedar Incident.

00:11:49.030 --> 00:11:52.430
At the very least, if your 
old man were still alive

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:55.440
things might be a little different.

00:11:56.010 --> 00:11:57.320
Really?

00:11:57.620 --> 00:11:59.160
The Nyoigatake Incident,

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:02.320
that was really something.

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:13.050
Transforming into a mountain is quite a feat.

00:12:13.910 --> 00:12:16.990
The look on the Kuramas' faces!

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:23.470
I haven't heard a story before or 
since where a tanuki cheated tengu.

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:26.450
Big Brother, Father was awesome, huh!

00:12:27.110 --> 00:12:30.700
For a tanuki, he was quite a guy.

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:35.470
Would you take Yakushibo 
with you on the leisure cruise?

00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:37.560
I'd like to come as well.

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:39.820
Okay, we'll plan on that.

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:41.630
Well then, I'll be off.

00:12:41.980 --> 00:12:45.030
Stay on your guard with Benten.

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:50.680
You can go home if you want.

00:12:50.990 --> 00:12:52.460
I'm going with you!

00:12:52.830 --> 00:12:55.790
Mom says I have to grow a backbone.

00:12:57.140 --> 00:12:58.250
In that case, let us be on our way.

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:08.760
<b>Nishizaki Genemon</b>

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:48.440
Is Benten at the clock tower?

00:14:48.980 --> 00:14:51.160
Indeed she is.

00:14:52.850 --> 00:14:55.610
The water has been rough lately,

00:14:55.850 --> 00:14:58.200
but we're having superb weather today.

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:31.120
Just as I thought, you can't handle it.

00:15:31.620 --> 00:15:35.570
Sorry Big Brother, I'm too 
scared to shape-shift.

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:40.520
It's not like Benten is eating 
tanuki hot pot all the time.

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:44.790
Well, whatever. 
Just relax and leave it to me.

00:15:56.300 --> 00:16:01.770
<b>Unrivaled Invincibility</b>

00:15:58.890 --> 00:15:59.960
Oh, how cute.

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:01.770
Your little brother?

00:16:10.590 --> 00:16:11.570
Thank you.

00:16:15.710 --> 00:16:18.670
You're looking awfully warm.

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:22.380
Couldn't you transform into something 
a little more refreshing for me?

00:16:22.850 --> 00:16:24.690
What's with that shirt?

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:27.460
It's not like you to have such bad taste.

00:16:27.910 --> 00:16:30.660
I got this from the Ebisugawa tanuki.

00:16:31.060 --> 00:16:32.590
You mean Kinkaku and Ginkaku?

00:16:32.850 --> 00:16:33.430
Yeah.

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:36.190
It came with this Electric Brandy.

00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:40.390
So, is there something 
I can help you with?

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:43.770
We'd like to borrow the inner parlor.

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:51.480
It's no laughing matter.

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:56.010
Just yesterday Kinkaku and Ginkaku came by

00:16:56.440 --> 00:16:58.860
and were saying that you 
would definitely come.

00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:03.570
They said they didn't want me poking 
my nose into a quarrel between tanuki

00:17:04.270 --> 00:17:07.800
and left this goofy t-shirt 
and Electric Brandy.

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:10.440
Pretty stingy bribe.

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:15.570
For real. If I wanted 
that stuff I could just take it.

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:19.410
Well, they're idiot brothers so that's about 
as good of a plan as they can come up with.

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:23.850
You want the inner parlor?

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:26.440
Like I've never wanted 
anything in my life.

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:28.290
Hm, what should I do...

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:32.650
Even if I lend it to you 
there's nothing in it for me.

00:17:35.730 --> 00:17:37.510
What are you up to today?

00:17:38.380 --> 00:17:39.800
Waiting for a whale.

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:42.270
There are whales around here?

00:17:42.990 --> 00:17:46.250
Sometimes they put in an 
appearance, out there.

00:17:47.360 --> 00:17:51.380
When I woke up this morning I suddenly felt 
like I wanted to try pulling a whale's tail.

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:53.540
That's why I'm here.

00:17:54.230 --> 00:17:58.030
But of course once you're waiting, 
they won't show up.

00:17:58.710 --> 00:18:00.280
Isn't that always the way.

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:01.710
Big Brother!

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:17.920
What's that?

00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:20.090
Take a look.

00:18:21.020 --> 00:18:24.370
I asked Mr. Genemon to 
repair the folding fan.

00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:28.740
You made a hole in it while you were
 pretending to be Nasu no Yoichi.

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:30.770
Had you forgotten?

00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:33.560
I've decided to avoid dwelling on the past.

00:18:34.220 --> 00:18:37.040
Bad tanuki, better think 
about what you've done.

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:15.620
I've made up my mind.

00:19:16.600 --> 00:19:20.010
Since you're the one asking, 
I'll let you use the inner parlor.

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:21.670
Thank you.

00:19:22.540 --> 00:19:26.760
But what'll we do if you 
ruin it like the folding fan?

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:29.500
You're such a rowdy one.

00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:31.190
I'll take good care of it!

00:19:31.700 --> 00:19:38.340
You better! If you wreck the inner parlor, 
I'll make you entertain the Friday Fellows.

00:19:39.210 --> 00:19:41.210
They were just asking me to line somebody up.

00:19:41.970 --> 00:19:46.530
And if you're boring, we'll just make you
 into a tanuki hot pot and devour you.

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:48.740
I don't taste very good.

00:19:49.210 --> 00:19:52.860
That's fine. I like you 
so much I want to eat you up.

00:19:58.670 --> 00:19:59.600
Look at that!

00:20:55.410 --> 00:20:58.310
Ready? Here is how you start it up.

00:21:21.390 --> 00:21:24.570
Even after Dad moved on to
 the afterlife, leaving us all too soon,

00:21:25.860 --> 00:21:29.130
Mom and us tanuki pups

00:21:29.710 --> 00:21:32.720
have launched a leisure cruiser each 
year on the night of the Fire Festival.

00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:38.870
Celebrating our Shimogamo ancestors? 
Doesn't even come to mind.

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:43.000
Sometimes we remember Dad,

00:21:43.470 --> 00:21:47.780
but mostly we just throw a crazy party.

00:21:49.030 --> 00:21:50.800
We're tanuki so that's what we do.

00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:57.380
It's another manifestation 
of our idiot blood.

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:33.510
It's the Gozan Fire Festival!

00:23:33.700 --> 00:23:34.910
Daimonji!

00:23:35.090 --> 00:23:36.350
We could take on a thousand foes!

00:23:36.950 --> 00:23:39.740
Enemies in the same boat!

00:23:37.700 --> 00:23:40.640
<b>Battle of the Daimonji Leisure Cruisers</b>
